---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import stickKey from '../assets/stick-key.png';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import BuyButton from '../components/BuyButton.astro';
import { updates } from '../data/updates';
import { site } from '../config';

/**
 * The founder note lived on the home page; this is its proper home.
 *
 * Everything here is either the founders' own words or a fact that can be
 * checked against the product. Nothing about the founding is invented, which
 * is why the page is short. It should get longer in their voice, not in ours.
 */
const first = updates[updates.length - 1];
---

<Base
  title="Our story | Stick"
  description="Why Stick works the way it does, from the two of us who built it."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-16 pb-14 md:pt-24">
    <h1 class="headline text-hero">Our story</h1>
    <p class="text-lead mt-9 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Stick exists because every blocker we tried kept its off switch within
      reach. Here is what came of that, in the words of the two of us who built
      it.
    </p>

    <Image
      src={stickKey}
      alt="The Stick key: a hot pink USB-C stick with Stick. embossed on it"
      widths={[520, 860, 1280]}
      sizes="(min-width: 768px) 48rem, 90vw"
      loading="eager"
      class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-xl mix-blend-multiply md:mt-16"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="rule bg-mist">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="space-y-5 text-[18px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <p>
          Every blocker we’d used had a way out, and we always took it. Not by
          defeating anything. By pressing the button the app handed us. Skip.
          Just this once. End session early.
        </p>
        <p>
          So the rule for Stick was: no button. A schedule can start a session
          but never end one, because an end time would be a way out that doesn’t
          need the key. Settings can’t be weakened while a session is running.
          There are five emergency unlocks for the times you really need one,
          they don’t refill, and we tell you they exist before you buy rather
          than letting you find them later.
        </p>
        <p>
          It’s also why it’s {site.price} once, with no subscription and nothing
          phoning home. You buy the object and then we leave you alone. Nothing
          in it has to hold your attention to keep earning its price, and
          nothing about it stops working if you never hear from us again.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink">
          It isn’t unbreakable. It’s your computer. What it is, is far enough
          away that the impulse usually doesn’t survive the walk.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-9 text-[16px] font-medium text-ink">
        Ben &amp; Noah, {site.company}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="headline text-display">What that turned into</h2>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Three rules, and every one of them costs us something:
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10">
      <div class="rule pt-6">
        <h3 class="text-[20px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          No way out that doesn’t involve walking
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Schedules can start a session and never end one. There is no timer to
          wait out and no early exit. It would have been easier to build the
          version with a button, and nobody would have complained.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rule pt-6">
        <h3 class="text-[20px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Tell people the limits before they pay
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Five emergency unlocks exist, they don’t refill, and we say so on the
          page where you buy rather than letting you discover it later. A
          product bought for self-control cannot afford to surprise anyone.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rule pt-6">
        <h3 class="text-[20px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]">
          Sell an object, then go away
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          The key is one payment and no subscription, and nothing in the app
          reports back to us. We don’t know what you block or how often,
          because there is no server of ours for it to reach.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rule bg-mist">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
      <h2 class="headline text-display">Still being built</h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        It started on {first.date} and it is not finished. We keep a dated log
        of what is happening, including the parts that go badly, because people
        are paying for this before it reaches their desk.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/updates"
        class="mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-ink px-6 py-3 text-[15px] font-medium transition-colors hover:bg-ink hover:text-white"
      >
        Read the updates
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:py-20">
    <h2 class="headline text-display">The only way out is a walk.</h2>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      {site.price} plus shipping, one time. Ships {site.shipWindow}.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-9">
      <BuyButton size="lg" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
